What is the difference between terraform state and terraform plan?
Can you also give a real-world example of when you would use each one?

terraform plan:
Purpose: Shows what Terraform will create, change, or destroy before applying changes.
Example: You want to add 2 new VMs in GCP. Before actually creating them, you run terraform plan to see exactly what Terraform will do — like checking the “before & after” picture of your infrastructure.

terraform state:
Purpose: Manages and views Terraform’s state file, which keeps track of the real-world resources Terraform has created.
Example: If you forget the name of a VM Terraform created, you can run:

terraform state list

to see all managed resources.
You can also use commands like terraform state show to view details of a specific resource.
💡 Key Difference:
plan = Preview future changes (doesn’t touch the infrastructure).
state = Look at the current reality Terraform knows about.
